WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.540
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:10.019
This RIF will be a bit different to normal,
I recently reached 100,000 subscribers, thanks

00:00:10.019 --> 00:00:14.750
to you guys, I couldn't have done it without
every single one of you.

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:19.010
Thank you for watching, liking, commenting
and sharing.

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:22.880
To celebrate, this RIF will be facts about
myself.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:29.160
I asked you on Facebook and Twitter what you
really want to know about Thoughty2, so here

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:36.050
we go.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:42.379
I'll start from the beginning, Kim and Matt
asked me, why did I start this channel?

00:00:42.379 --> 00:00:49.100
For as long as I can remember I've been interested
in facts, the more useless the better.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:54.930
I've always researched and asked questions,
about absolutely everything, when I come across

00:00:54.930 --> 00:01:01.399
something in life that I don't know or understand,
I have to know... why, when, who and what's

00:01:01.399 --> 00:01:03.100
it all about.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:07.690
So a couple of years ago I thought, why don't
I share my passion for knowledge with the

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:14.040
world, and along the way if I can make a living
out of doing what I love, then, well isn't

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.860
that everyone's dream.

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:22.080
When I uploaded my first video my expectations
were low, The idea of more than 10 people

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:27.600
watching it seemed alien to me, I was in no
way prepared for the enormity of views that

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:29.580
followed over the next year.

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:32.630
And I still can't quite believe my good fortune.

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:36.070
Evan Wright asked, where do I live?

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:42.200
I grew up in and to this day, still live,
in a region in the north of England called

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:49.170
Lancashire, which is famous for bringing the
world the industrial revolution and The Beatles.

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:52.830
Laura and Ali asked how old am I?

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:55.380
Thanks for asking, I'm 22.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:59.400
Morgan Jerome asked what is my favourite food.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:05.980
That's a tricky question, but it's probably
Marmite on toast, it's really popular in the

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:12.090
United Kingdom but if you've never tasted
it before, be prepared for a shock.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:17.600
Mark Pliner asked how many people are working
on the show.

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:23.390
It's just me, from research to design, filming
and editing, I'm all on my own.

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:30.390
Of course I have the moral support of my fans,
and my family and friends, whom all motivate

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:34.780
me to make my videos as good as they possibly
can be.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:41.320
Steve Cancel asked what did I study at University
and what is my day job?

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:47.250
I didn't go to university, it was never a
possibility for me, not because I couldn't,

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:50.480
but because I didn't want to.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:54.910
Which may come as a surprise from someone
who claims to be so enthralled by knowledge

00:02:54.910 --> 00:02:56.240
and facts.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:02.520
But I have always preferred to do things my
own way, from the moment I left college, I

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:09.300
was determined to do something significant
and most importantly, do something that I

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:10.300
love.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:14.520
To me University seemed like an impediment
of that goal.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:17.820
The skills I have learnt have all been self
taught.

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:20.090
So, do I have a job?

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:22.350
Yes, it's called Thoughty2.

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:27.090
Before I started this channel I managed a
small team in the advertising department of

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:34.420
a retail company, but I quit that job to start
Thoughty2, because I wanted to do something

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:38.100
I enjoy and advertising wasn't it.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:44.860
It was an enormous risk, but I couldn't be
happier doing anything else than making interesting

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:49.550
videos about the weirdest and wackiest topics
I can possibly think of.

00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:55.790
And the fact that so many people enjoy watching
my videos is more fulfilling than any day

00:03:55.790 --> 00:04:00.380
job I previously had, could have ever offered.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:04.980
Tim Best asked what was my favourite subject
in school?

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:07.040
My favourite subject was physics.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:13.810
But I also really enjoyed art, to this day,
I still draw a lot in my spare time.

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:16.519
Mary asked who is my favourite scientist?

00:04:16.519 --> 00:04:18.320
There are so many great individuals whom have
shaped the face of science, that I don't believe

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:21.010
one can be called the best or the greatest.

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:28.320
But my personal favourite is Stephen Hawking,
whom despite immense difficulties has pioneered

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:32.070
some of the greatest scientific discoveries
the world has ever known.

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:37.660
Hawking has done incredible work on black
holes over his lifetime, which is a personal

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:39.050
interest of mine.

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:42.410
Billy Stanley asked "How do you think up such
thoughts?

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:45.150
Is it down to research or prior knowledge?".

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:51.870
Well, honestly it's a mix of both, like I
mentioned earlier, I have always had an insatiable

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:54.230
appetite for knowledge and learning.

00:04:54.230 --> 00:05:00.370
But I can't for a moment pretend that I already
know every fact that I put into my videos,

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:06.900
an awful lot of research goes into creating
each episode, which I thoroughly enjoy, because

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:09.930
I learn a lot of new things along the way.

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:16.419
Taylor Wyler and Jon asked "Where did you
come up with the name Thoughty2"?.

00:05:16.419 --> 00:05:17.940
It's a pun.

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:23.810
The comedy science fiction series The Hitchhiker's
Guide to the Galaxy by Douglas Adams suggests

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:29.900
that the answer to the ultimate question of
life, the universe and everything is simply

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:31.840
42.

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:35.900
This anecdote has has since found it's way
into international geekdom.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:41.690
And it is a popular joke amongst geeks and
science fiction fans the world over, that

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:48.240
the universally accepted answer to the question
of the meaning of life, the universe and everything

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.820
is 42.

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:56.330
Even Google agrees, when you Google "The answer
to life the universe and everything" Google's

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:59.970
calculator will present you with the number
42.

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:05.699
So yes, Kristen Graf, I am secretly saying
42.

00:06:05.699 --> 00:06:15.139
And finally Alex, Gambler_182, Milone, Thomas
and Jonathan all asked what's my real name.

00:06:15.139 --> 00:06:22.490
My name is Arran, spelt with a double R. Which
is of Scottish origin, the name originates

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:24.800
from the Isle of Arran.

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:31.229
I want to finish by thanking you all for your
support, it really wouldn't be possible without

00:06:31.229 --> 00:06:33.919
you, so thank you.

00:06:33.919 --> 00:06:36.879
And of course, thanks for the view, subscribe
for more Thoughty2.

